Router: fix the routing API data race at the pin without stalling route picks

FORK DEVIATION: not upstream code. Upstream fixes the same race with a larger refactor that
does not apply to the pin; this follows its shape. The rules and balancers are published
together as one immutable table behind an atomic pointer, so PickRoute, ListRule and balancer
lookups take no lock. ReloadRules and RemoveRule are serialized by the router mutex, build a
new table from the current one, publish it with one atomic store and close the webhooks of
replaced or removed rules after the mutex is released. A failed ReloadRules publishes nothing.

